p time.\",\n    78→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    79→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.78\",\n    80→    \"date\": \"2026-03-17\",\n    81→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    82→  },\n    83→  {\n    84→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    85→    \"title\": \"v2.1.77\",\n    86→    \"description\": \"Increased maximum output token limits for Claude Opus 4.6 to 64k tokens default and 128k tokens upper bound. Added allowRead sandbox setting and optional index for /copy. Fixed Always Allow on compound commands, auto-updater memory issues, resume truncation, PreToolUse permission bypass, CRLF line ending conversion, and beta headers.\",\n    87→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    88→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.77\",\n    89→    \"date\": \"2026-03-17\",\n    90→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    94→    \"title\": \"Self-hosted Cloud Agents\",\n    95→    \"description\": \"Cursor now supports self-hosted cloud agents that keep code and tool execution entirely in your own network. Your codebase, build outputs, and secrets all stay on internal machines running in your infrastructure, while the agent handles tool calls locally. Self-hosted cloud agents offer the same capabilities as Cursor-hosted cloud agents, including isolated VMs, full development environments, multi-model harnesses, and plugins.\",\n    96→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog/03-25-26\",\n    98→    \"date\": \"2026-03-25\",\n    99→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   100→  },\n   101→  {\n   102→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   103→    \"title\": \"Composer 2\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Composer 2 is now available in Cursor, offering frontier-level coding performance with strong results on CursorBench, Terminal-Bench 2.0, and SWE-bench Multilingual. The model delivers large improvements over previous versions with scores of 61.3 on CursorBench, 61.7 on Terminal-Bench 2.0, and 73.7 on SWE-bench Multilingual. It's priced at $0.50/M input and $2.50/M output tokens, with a faster variant available at $1.50/M input and $7.50/M output tokens.\",\n   105→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   106→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog/composer-2\",\n   107→    \"date\": \"2026-03-19\",\n   108→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   109→  },\n   110→  {\n   111→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   112→    \"title\": \"Create issues from Slack with Copilot\",\n   113→    \"description\": \"You can now create GitHub Issues directly from Slack using natural language with the GitHub app for Slack. Mention @GitHub in any channel, describe the work you need to track, and Copilot will automatically create a properly formatted issue.\",\n   114→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   115→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-30-create-issues-from-slack-with-copilot\",\n   116→    \"date\": \"2026-03-30\",\n   117→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   118→  },\n   119→  {\n   120→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   121→    \"title\": \"Ask @copilot to resolve merge conflicts on pull requests\",\n   122→    \"description\": \"Copilot coding agent can now resolve merge conflicts on pull requests. Simply mention @copilot in a comment and tell it to resolve the conflicts, and it will attempt to fix them automatically.\",\n   123→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   124→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-26-ask-copilot-to-resolve-merge-conflicts-on-pull-requests\",\n   125→    \"date\": \"2026-03-26\",\n   126→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   127→  },\n   128→  {\n   129→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   130→    \"title\": \"Copilot usage metrics now identify active Copilot coding agent users\",\n   131→    \"description\": \"Copilot usage metrics now indicate which users have Copilot coding agent (CCA) activity. Enterprise and organization admins can identify which users are actively using Copilot coding agent on daily and weekly bases through improved metrics dashboards.\",\n   132→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   133→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-25-copilot-usage-metrics-now-identify-active-copilot-coding-agent-users\",\n   134→    \"date\": \"2026-03-25\",\n   135→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   136→  },\n   137→  {\n   138→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   139→    \"title\": \"GitHub Copilot for Jira — Public preview enhancements\",\n   140→    \"description\": \"Since launching the public preview of GitHub Copilot coding agent for Jira, GitHub has made enhancements based on customer feedback. Copilot now includes Jira ticket numbers in PR titles and branch names, adds links back to originating Jira tickets, and includes Jira context provided to the agent.\",\n   141→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   142→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-25-github-copilot-for-jira-public-preview-enhancements\",\n   143→    \"date\": \"2026-03-25\",\n   144→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   145→  },\n   146→  {\n   147→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   148→    \"title\": \"Ask @copilot to make changes to a pull request\",\n   149→    \"description\": \"You can now mention @copilot in pull requests to ask Copilot to make changes. It can fix failing GitHub Actions workflows, address review comments, refactor code, and update documentation based on your instructions.\",\n   150→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   151→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-24-ask-copilot-to-make-changes-to-any-pull-request\",\n   152→    \"date\": \"2026-03-24\",\n   153→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   154→  },\n   155→  {\n   156→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   157→    \"title\": \"Manage Copilot coding agent repository access via the API\",\n   158→    \"description\": \"Organization owners can now manage Copilot coding agent access at scale programmatically with new Copilot coding agent management REST APIs, available in public preview. This enables automation of repository access permissions for Copilot agents.\",\n   159→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   160→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-24-manage-copilot-coding-agent-repository-access-via-the-api\",\n   161→    \"date\": \"2026-03-24\",\n   162→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   163→  },\n   164→  {\n   165→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   166→    \"title\": \"Devin can now Schedule Devins\",\n   167→    \"description\": \"Devin can now schedule its own recurring sessions to handle repetitive tasks like weekly release notes, feature flag cleanups, and QA sweeps. Users can run a task once, and if successful, tell Devin to keep doing it on a schedule. Devin maintains state between runs, so each session picks up where the last one left off, building on context rather than starting from scratch.\",\n   168→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   169→    \"url\": \"https://cognition.ai/blog/devin-can-now-schedule-devins\",\n   170→    \"date\": \"2026-03-20\",\n   171→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   172→  },\n   173→  {\n   174→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   175→    \"title\": \"Devin can now Manage Devins\",\n   176→    \"description\": \"Devin can now break down large tasks and delegate them to a team of managed Devins that work in parallel. Each managed Devin runs in its own isolated virtual machine with its own terminal, browser, and development environment. The main Devin acts as a coordinator, scoping work, assigning tasks, monitoring progress, resolving conflicts, and compiling results.\",\n   177→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   178→    \"url\": \"https://cognition.ai/blog/devin-can-now-manage-devins\",\n   179→    \"date\": \"2026-03-19\",\n   180→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"productName\": \"Aider\",\n   184→    \"title\": \"GPT-5.3 and GPT-5.4 Model Support Added\",\n   185→    \"description\": \"Aider added support for new OpenAI GPT-5.3 and GPT-5.4 model variants across OpenAI, Azure, and OpenRouter providers. This includes both chat and codex variants, expanding the suite of GPT-5 models available to users.\",\n   186→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/commit/c41ef3b\",\n   188→    \"date\": \"2026-03-17\",\n   189→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   190→  },\n   191→  {\n   192→    \"productName\": \"Aider\",\n   193→    \"title\": \"Exception Handling Improvements\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Added ExInfo for PermissionDeniedError to improve error handling and mapping. Fixed exception mapping to only include real exception classes, avoiding runtime errors. Contributed by Claudia Pellegrino.\",\n   195→    \"updateType\": \"bugfix\",\n   196→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/commit/38716cc\",\n   197→    \"date\": \"2026-03-17\",\n   198→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   199→  },\n   200→  {\n   201→    \"productName\": \"Aider\",\n   202→    \"title\": \"Deprecated Models Removed from Tests\",\n   203→    \"description\": \"Replaced deprecated models (gpt-4-32k, claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620, and gpt-4-vision-preview) in unit tests with currently available alternatives to ensure tests pass correctly.\",\n   204→    \"updateType\": \"bugfix\",\n   205→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/pull/4935\",\n   206→    \"date\": \"2026-03-16\",\n   207→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   208→  },\n   209→  {\n   210→    \"productName\": \"Aider\",\n   211→    \"title\": \"Main Branch Features (Unreleased)\",\n   212→    \"description\": \"The main branch contains unreleased features including: Claude 4.5/4.6 model support, expanded Gemini support (2.5 Flash, Flash-Lite, and Gemini 3 preview), DeepSeek Reasoner model, new `/ok` command shortcut, and support for GPT-5.1/5.2/5.3/5.4 variants across multiple providers. Aider wrote 62% of the code in this upcoming release.\",\n   213→    \"updateType\": \"announcement\",\n   214→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/blob/main/HISTORY.md\",\n   215→    \"date\": \"2026-03-17\",\n   216→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   217→  }\n   218→]\n   219→"
      }
    ]
